{
  "$comment": [
    "THE sx VOCABULARY. One table. The lint reads it, the TS types generate from it,",
    "the docs reference generates from it, the LSP completions come from it, and the",
    "agent SKILL.md is written from it. Adding a property is one row, not a code change",
    "in four places.",
    "",
    "Names are Tailwind's, because that is the prior every agent already has, and it is",
    "terse (an agent pays for every character). Values are OURS: a token name from a",
    "scale, or a CSS keyword. Never a raw number, never a colour, never a unit.",
    "",
    "Two kinds of utility:",
    "  scale:    the value IS a design decision. A token from that scale, and nothing else.",
    "  keywords: the value is physics, with no design opinion. The CSS keywords, all of them.",
    "",
    "The allowlist was the mistake. The value discipline is the point."
  ],

  "scales": {
    "$comment": "Resolved from the token registry (tokens.css) — sx can never drift from the theme.",
    "space": "@tokens:space-*",
    "size": "@tokens:size-*",
    "color": "@tokens:color-surface",
    "radius": "@tokens:radius-*",
    "border-width": "@tokens:border-*",
    "text": "@tokens:text-*",
    "weight": "@tokens:weight-*",
    "font": "@tokens:font-*",
    "leading": "@tokens:leading-*",
    "tracking": "@tokens:tracking-*",
    "shadow": "@tokens:shadow-*",
    "z": "@tokens:z-*",
    "opacity": "@tokens:opacity-*",
    "angle": "@tokens:angle-*",
    "duration": "@tokens:duration-*",
    "ease": "@tokens:ease-*",
    "breakpoint": "@tokens:breakpoint-*"
  },

  "$missing_scales": [
    "size-*        dimensions above the space scale. space tops out near 40px; both media",
    "              components wanted 48px, the canvas wanted 180 and 320. Nothing to spend.",
    "border-*      every border in sx lowers to 1px. A 3px category stripe is unsayable.",
    "angle-*       rotate speaks 0/45/90/180/270. A 1deg tilt is unsayable.",
    "opacity-*     steps of 25 cannot say a bar chart's 0.85 rest state.",
    "A closed vocabulary is only fair if the vocabulary is complete. These are token-registry",
    "work, and they are the reason every wall was a wall."
  ],

  "utilities": {
    "$spacing": null,
    "p":  { "css": ["padding"], "scale": "space" },
    "px": { "css": ["padding-inline"], "scale": "space" },
    "py": { "css": ["padding-block"], "scale": "space" },
    "pt": { "css": ["padding-top"], "scale": "space" },
    "pr": { "css": ["padding-right"], "scale": "space" },
    "pb": { "css": ["padding-bottom"], "scale": "space" },
    "pl": { "css": ["padding-left"], "scale": "space" },
    "ps": { "css": ["padding-inline-start"], "scale": "space" },
    "pe": { "css": ["padding-inline-end"], "scale": "space" },

    "m":  { "css": ["margin"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "mx": { "css": ["margin-inline"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "my": { "css": ["margin-block"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "mt": { "css": ["margin-top"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "mr": { "css": ["margin-right"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "mb": { "css": ["margin-bottom"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "ml": { "css": ["margin-left"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "ms": { "css": ["margin-inline-start"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "me": { "css": ["margin-inline-end"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },

    "inset":   { "css": ["inset"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "inset-x": { "css": ["inset-inline"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "inset-y": { "css": ["inset-block"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "top":     { "css": ["top"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "right":   { "css": ["right"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "bottom":  { "css": ["bottom"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },
    "left":    { "css": ["left"], "scale": "space", "keywords": ["auto"], "negatable": true },

    "$sizing": null,
    "w":     { "css": ["width"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["auto", "full", "screen", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "min-w": { "css": ["min-width"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["0", "full", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "max-w": { "css": ["max-width"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["none", "full", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "h":     { "css": ["height"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["auto", "full", "screen", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "min-h": { "css": ["min-height"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["0", "full", "screen", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "max-h": { "css": ["max-height"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["none", "full", "screen", "fit", "min", "max"] },
    "size":  { "css": ["width", "height"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["auto", "full", "fit"] },
    "basis": { "css": ["flex-basis"], "scale": "size", "keywords": ["auto", "full", "0"] },
    "aspect": { "css": ["aspect-ratio"], "keywords": ["auto", "square", "video"] },

    "$colour": null,
    "bg":         { "css": ["background-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "text":       { "css": ["color"], "scale": "color", "overloads": ["text-size", "text-align"] },
    "border":     { "css": ["border-color"], "scale": "color", "overloads": ["border-width", "border-style"] },
    "border-t":   { "css": ["border-top-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "border-r":   { "css": ["border-right-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "border-b":   { "css": ["border-bottom-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "border-l":   { "css": ["border-left-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "outline":    { "css": ["outline-color"], "scale": "color", "overloads": ["outline-width", "outline-style"] },
    "ring":       { "css": ["--ring-color"], "scale": "color", "$note": "lowers to the framework's box-shadow ring" },
    "fill":       { "css": ["fill"], "scale": "color", "keywords": ["none", "currentColor"] },
    "stroke":     { "css": ["stroke"], "scale": "color", "keywords": ["none", "currentColor"] },
    "caret":      { "css": ["caret-color"], "scale": "color" },
    "accent":     { "css": ["accent-color"], "scale": "color", "keywords": ["auto"] },
    "decoration": { "css": ["text-decoration-color"], "scale": "color", "overloads": ["decoration-style"] },

    "$typography": null,
    "text-size":  { "css": ["font-size"], "scale": "text", "$name": "text", "$disambiguate": "value is on the text scale" },
    "font":       { "css": ["font-family"], "scale": "font", "overloads": ["font-weight", "font-style"] },
    "font-weight": { "css": ["font-weight"], "scale": "weight", "$name": "font", "$disambiguate": "value is on the weight scale" },
    "leading":    { "css": ["line-height"], "scale": "leading" },
    "tracking":   { "css": ["letter-spacing"], "scale": "tracking" },
    "indent":     { "css": ["text-indent"], "scale": "space" },
    "text-align": { "css": ["text-align"], "keywords": ["left", "center", "right", "justify", "start", "end"], "$name": "text" },
    "whitespace": { "css": ["white-space"], "keywords": ["normal", "nowrap", "pre", "pre-line", "pre-wrap", "break-spaces"] },
    "break":      { "css": ["overflow-wrap", "word-break"], "keywords": ["normal", "words", "all", "keep"] },
    "truncate":   { "css": ["overflow", "text-overflow", "white-space"], "composite": ["hidden", "ellipsis", "nowrap"] },
    "case":       { "css": ["text-transform"], "keywords": ["uppercase", "lowercase", "capitalize", "normal-case"], "$bare": true },
    "italic":     { "css": ["font-style"], "keywords": ["italic", "not-italic"], "$bare": true },
    "underline":  { "css": ["text-decoration-line"], "keywords": ["underline", "overline", "line-through", "no-underline"], "$bare": true },
    "nums":       { "css": ["font-variant-numeric"], "keywords": ["normal-nums", "ordinal", "slashed-zero", "lining-nums", "oldstyle-nums", "proportional-nums", "tabular-nums"], "$bare": true },
    "list":       { "css": ["list-style-type"], "keywords": ["none", "disc", "decimal"] },
    "align":      { "css": ["vertical-align"], "keywords": ["baseline", "top", "middle", "bottom", "text-top", "text-bottom", "sub", "super"] },

    "$borders": null,
    "rounded":    { "css": ["border-radius"], "scale": "radius", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "rounded-t":  { "css": ["border-start-start-radius", "border-start-end-radius"], "scale": "radius", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "rounded-b":  { "css": ["border-end-start-radius", "border-end-end-radius"], "scale": "radius", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "rounded-l":  { "css": ["border-start-start-radius", "border-end-start-radius"], "scale": "radius", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "rounded-r":  { "css": ["border-start-end-radius", "border-end-end-radius"], "scale": "radius", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "border-width":   { "css": ["border-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "border", "$disambiguate": "value is on the border-width scale" },
    "border-t-width": { "css": ["border-top-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "border-t" },
    "border-r-width": { "css": ["border-right-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "border-r" },
    "border-b-width": { "css": ["border-bottom-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "border-b" },
    "border-l-width": { "css": ["border-left-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "border-l" },
    "border-style":   { "css": ["border-style"], "keywords": ["solid", "dashed", "dotted", "double", "hidden", "none"], "$name": "border" },
    "outline-width":  { "css": ["outline-width"], "scale": "border-width", "$name": "outline" },
    "outline-style":  { "css": ["outline-style"], "keywords": ["none", "solid", "dashed", "dotted", "double"], "$name": "outline" },
    "outline-offset": { "css": ["outline-offset"], "scale": "space" },

    "$effects": null,
    "shadow":     { "css": ["box-shadow"], "scale": "shadow", "keywords": ["none"] },
    "opacity":    { "css": ["opacity"], "scale": "opacity" },
    "mix-blend":  { "css": ["mix-blend-mode"], "keywords": ["normal", "multiply", "screen", "overlay", "darken", "lighten", "difference", "exclusion", "luminosity"] },
    "isolate":    { "css": ["isolation"], "keywords": ["isolate", "auto"], "$bare": true },

    "$transitions": {
      "$note": [
        "sx owns the everyday transition: a property easing when it changes. Values are",
        "tokens, so a duration can never be a raw 137ms. `motion:` owns what CSS cannot do",
        "— springs, scroll timelines, staggers, FLIP. Two jobs, not one confused one."
      ]
    },
    "transition": { "css": ["transition-property"], "keywords": ["none", "all", "colors", "opacity", "shadow", "transform"] },
    "duration":   { "css": ["transition-duration"], "scale": "duration" },
    "ease":       { "css": ["transition-timing-function"], "scale": "ease" },
    "delay":      { "css": ["transition-delay"], "scale": "duration" },

    "$transforms": null,
    "rotate":      { "css": ["rotate"], "scale": "angle", "negatable": true },
    "scale":       { "css": ["scale"], "scale": "opacity", "$note": "percentage scale, shares the 0-100 ramp" },
    "translate-x": { "css": ["translate"], "scale": "space", "negatable": true },
    "translate-y": { "css": ["translate"], "scale": "space", "negatable": true },
    "origin":      { "css": ["transform-origin"], "keywords": ["center", "top", "top-right", "right", "bottom-right", "bottom", "bottom-left", "left", "top-left"] },

    "$box": {
      "$note": "The element's OWN box. How its children sit is <row>/<column>/<grid> — never sx."
    },
    "display":  { "css": ["display"], "keywords": ["block", "inline-block", "inline", "hidden", "contents", "flow-root", "list-item"], "$bare": true, "$refused": ["flex", "grid", "inline-flex", "inline-grid"], "$refused_because": "a layout context is a layout element — <row>, <column>, <grid>, <stack>" },
    "position": { "css": ["position"], "keywords": ["static", "relative", "absolute", "fixed", "sticky"], "$bare": true },
    "z":        { "css": ["z-index"], "scale": "z", "keywords": ["auto"] },
    "overflow":   { "css": ["overflow"], "keywords": ["auto", "hidden", "clip", "visible", "scroll"] },
    "overflow-x": { "css": ["overflow-x"], "keywords": ["auto", "hidden", "clip", "visible", "scroll"] },
    "overflow-y": { "css": ["overflow-y"], "keywords": ["auto", "hidden", "clip", "visible", "scroll"] },
    "object":     { "css": ["object-fit"], "keywords": ["contain", "cover", "fill", "none", "scale-down"], "overloads": ["object-position"] },
    "object-position": { "css": ["object-position"], "keywords": ["center", "top", "right", "bottom", "left"], "$name": "object" },
    "box":        { "css": ["box-sizing"], "keywords": ["border", "content"] },
    "visible":    { "css": ["visibility"], "keywords": ["visible", "invisible", "collapse"], "$bare": true },
    "sr-only":    { "css": ["position", "width", "height", "padding", "margin", "overflow", "clip-path", "white-space", "border-width"], "composite": ["absolute", "1px", "1px", "0", "-1px", "hidden", "inset(50%)", "nowrap", "0"], "$bare": true, "$note": "hidden to the eye, present to assistive tech. Every graphic owes its reader a text alternative; this is where they live." },

    "$self": {
      "$note": "The child's own participation in its parent's layout. The PARENT decides arrangement."
    },
    "grow":   { "css": ["flex-grow"], "keywords": ["0", "1"] },
    "shrink": { "css": ["flex-shrink"], "keywords": ["0", "1"] },
    "order":  { "css": ["order"], "keywords": ["first", "last", "none"] },
    "self":   { "css": ["align-self"], "keywords": ["auto", "start", "center", "end", "stretch", "baseline"] },
    "justify-self": { "css": ["justify-self"], "keywords": ["auto", "start", "center", "end", "stretch"] },

    "$interactivity": null,
    "cursor":         { "css": ["cursor"], "keywords": ["auto", "default", "pointer", "wait", "text", "move", "help", "not-allowed", "none", "context-menu", "progress", "cell", "crosshair", "vertical-text", "alias", "copy", "no-drop", "grab", "grabbing", "all-scroll", "col-resize", "row-resize", "n-resize", "e-resize", "s-resize", "w-resize", "ew-resize", "ns-resize", "zoom-in", "zoom-out"] },
    "select":         { "css": ["user-select"], "keywords": ["none", "text", "all", "auto"] },
    "pointer-events": { "css": ["pointer-events"], "keywords": ["none", "auto"] },
    "touch":          { "css": ["touch-action"], "keywords": ["auto", "none", "pan-x", "pan-y", "pinch-zoom", "manipulation"] },
    "resize":         { "css": ["resize"], "keywords": ["none", "y", "x", "both"] },
    "appearance":     { "css": ["appearance"], "keywords": ["none", "auto"] },
    "scroll":         { "css": ["scroll-behavior"], "keywords": ["auto", "smooth"] },
    "will-change":    { "css": ["will-change"], "keywords": ["auto", "scroll", "contents", "transform"] },
    "contain":        { "css": ["contain"], "keywords": ["none", "content", "strict", "size", "layout", "paint"] }
  },

  "prefixes": {
    "$comment": "Closed. A visual state is reachable ONLY by stamping the semantics an assistive technology also reads. That is what makes the accessible component the cheapest one to build.",
    "state": ["hover", "focus", "focus-within", "focus-visible", "active", "disabled", "current", "selected", "expanded", "busy", "checked", "pressed", "open"],
    "group": "group-<state>  — a descendant reads its host's state",
    "value": "state-<value>  — on the one reserved data-state attribute",
    "condition": ["mobile", "tablet", "desktop", "motion-reduce", "motion-safe", "forced-colors", "print"]
  },

  "refused": {
    "$comment": "An author must be able to tell a PRINCIPLE from a TODO. Today they cannot, so both read as the language fighting them. Every one of these must name its replacement — the mission is never 'find another way'.",
    "flex-direction | justify-content | align-items | flex-wrap | gap | grid-template-*": "<row> / <column> / <grid> / <stack> / <center> — the parent decides arrangement, and the vocabulary is closed so two authors cannot diverge",
    "display: flex | grid": "that IS <row> / <grid>",
    "@keyframes | animation": "motion: — springs, scroll, stagger, FLIP",
    "selectors of any kind": "state prefixes, keyed on ARIA",
    "arbitrary values (16px, #3366ff, 1.35)": "a token. The compiler prints the scale.",
    "!important": "nothing. There is no cascade to fight — sx attaches to one element."
  }
}
